  "statementTechnical": "Orientation admits only two values: σ ∈ {+1, -1}. Macroscopic moral ambiguity maps to quantum superposition of fundamental binary micro-states. [DEFENSE REQUIRED: The binary claim depends on an underlying symmetry group (SU(2)) that grounds two-state behavior. This is a modeling choice, not a deduction. If continuous moral state space with different topology exists, the binary reduction might not hold. Full defense required in Appendix C: Moral Symmetry Argument.]",
  "statementPlain": "Orientation admits only two values: σ ∈ {+1, -1}. Macroscopic moral ambiguity maps to quantum superposition of fundamental binary micro-states. [DEFENSE REQUIRED: The binary claim depends on an underlying symmetry group (SU(2)) that grounds two-state behavior. This is a modeling choice, not a deduction. If continuous moral state space with different topology exists, the binary reduction might not hold. Full defense required in Appendix C: Moral Symmetry Argument.]",
  "mathematicalForm": "σ̂ = diag(1,-1); σ ∈ {+1,-1}; no σ = 0",
